      "message": "Thanks for providing the doc. It\u0027s fine. But I am not sure if it\u0027s addressed reporter\u0027s concern. For the broadcast, we had doc says that \"A change in network connectivity has occurred. A default connection has either been established or lost.\". This should notify the default connection change. Tethering state is not the case I think. Of course clearer documentation will always help but I wonder if we need to list all the unspported cases/conditions. Or we could say it\u0027s supported in other services?",
